Goal references in an imported body: the body reaches its engine as written, with no make
expansion, so every dollar sign is the guest's, and the one form amk reads in it is a
name between two at signs, of letters, digits, underscore, dot, dash and slash. The
references are recorded at import and resolved once the makefiles are read, before any
job starts, so a reference may precede the define it names. A name matches in any case
and must match exactly one target a makefile names, bare or under the value directory,
whatever files are on disk: none is fatal, and so are two that differ only in case. Each
reference is a prerequisite on the goal's value file, and in the job's fork it becomes
the value's text, raw, less one trailing newline. The goal function stays for ordinary
rules and recipes, where the text is make's.

